---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Latch Tools"
  description="Latch Tools processes all files locally in your browser. No uploads, no tracking, no stored data. Read the full privacy policy."
  ogImage="/og/privacy-policy.png"
>
  <Header />

  <main>
    <section class="section" style="padding-bottom: 0">
      <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 780px">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="bar"></span>Legal</span>
        <h1 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -.03em; line-height: 1.06; font-size: clamp(30px, 4.5vw, 44px); margin: 18px 0 0;">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p style="color: var(--text-3); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13px; margin: 14px 0 40px;">
          Last updated: 2 June 2026
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
      <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 680px">
        <div class="prose">

          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <p>
            Latch converts and processes your files entirely inside your browser.
            No file — not a single byte of its content — is ever sent to our servers
            or any third party. We cannot access your files, and we do not try to.
          </p>

          <h2>What we do <em>not</em> collect</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Your files or any part of their content.</li>
            <li>Filenames, file sizes, or metadata about files you process.</li>
            <li>Conversion results or downloads.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            All processing happens using your device's own CPU and browser APIs
            (Canvas, WebAssembly, JavaScript). The results are created locally and
            downloaded directly to your device.
          </p>

          <h2>What Cloudflare Pages collects</h2>
          <p>
            Latch is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. When you visit the site, Cloudflare's
            infrastructure records standard server access data: your IP address,
            user-agent string, the page requested, and the timestamp. This is typical
            of any web server and is not specific to Latch.
          </p>
          <p>
            These logs are used for security, abuse prevention, and uptime monitoring.
            They are not linked to individuals, not sold, and not used for advertising.
            See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-text)">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a> for details.
          </p>

          <h2>Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            Latch sets no cookies. The one measurement tool it uses — Cloudflare Web
            Analytics (see below) — is cookieless and stores nothing on your device, so
            no consent banner is required. If cookie-based analytics or advertising are
            ever added, this policy will be updated before any such scripts are enabled,
            and a compliant consent banner will be shown to visitors in the UK and EU.
          </p>

          <h2>Analytics</h2>
          <p>
            Latch uses <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-text)">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>,
            a privacy-first service that measures aggregate page views and performance.
            It is cookieless, sets nothing on your device, does not fingerprint you, and
            collects no personal data or cross-site identifiers. It also cannot see or
            access the files you work with — all file processing stays in your browser and
            never reaches any analytics script.
          </p>

          <h2>Third-party scripts</h2>
          <p>
            Fonts are self-hosted, so no third-party font service is contacted. The only
            third-party script Latch loads is the cookieless Cloudflare Web Analytics
            beacon described above, which cannot access the files you work with. No other
            third-party scripts are loaded.
          </p>

          <h2>Your rights (UK &amp; EU)</h2>
          <p>
            Because we do not collect personal data beyond standard Cloudflare server
            logs (which we do not control or process ourselves), there is no personal
            data held by Latch for you to access, correct, or erase.
            If you have questions, contact us at the address below.
          </p>

          <h2>Children</h2>
          <p>
            Latch is a general-purpose utility and does not knowingly collect data from
            children under 13 (or the relevant age of digital consent in your jurisdiction).
          </p>

          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            If this policy changes in a meaningful way — for example, when analytics
            or ads are introduced — the "last updated" date at the top will change and
            we will describe what is new. Continued use of the site after a material
            change constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Questions or concerns about this policy:
            <a href="mailto:privacy@latchtools.com" style="color: var(--accent-text)">privacy@latchtools.com</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 20px;
    letter-spacing: -.02em;
    margin: 44px 0 12px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .prose h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .prose p {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    max-width: 64ch;
  }
  .prose ul {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
    padding-left: 22px;
  }
  .prose ul li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .prose em { font-style: italic; }
</style>
